<rml>
<head>
	<title>Doppelganger frame (CDoppelGangerFrame)</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="base.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="doppelganger_frame.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="doppelganger_frame">
	<!-- The Doppelganger event HUD (CDoppelGangerFrame): the frame, the monsters that passed, "Time
	     left", the time, the monsters' progress gauge (yellow, orange, red by how many passed), the
	     Ice Walker's marker and the party members' markers on the path. A LayoutMode::Hud window, so
	     .screen is the 640x480 reference screen stretched W/640 x H/480 like the original and #panel
	     sits at the window's reference position. Text does not stretch: each line takes its native
	     size and cancels the stretch. In the background context, behind its other documents (the
	     original drew it under every panel). Takes no pointer events. -->
	<div class="screen" data-style-transform="'scale(' + scale_x + ', ' + scale_y + ')'">
		<div id="panel" data-style-left="panel_x + 'px'" data-style-top="panel_y + 'px'">
			<div id="back"></div>
			<span class="frame-text" data-for="t : texts" data-class-big="t.big" data-style-top="t.top + 'px'"
			      data-style-color="t.color" data-style-font-size="t.text_px + 'px'"
			      data-style-width="(110 * scale_x) + 'px'"
			      data-style-transform="'scale(' + inverse_scale_x + ', ' + inverse_scale_y + ')'">{{t.text}}</span>
			<img class="bar" data-for="b : bars" data-attr-src="b.src" data-attr-rect="b.rect"
			     data-style-left="b.left + 'px'" data-style-width="b.width + 'px'"/>
			<img id="icewalker" src="../../../Double_Micon01.tga" data-if="ice_walker_visible"
			     data-style-left="ice_walker_left + 'px'"/>
			<div class="marker" data-for="m : markers" data-class-hero="m.hero" data-style-left="m.left + 'px'"></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
